What does this print?
```ruby
compose = ->(f, g) { ->(x) { g.(f.(x)) } }
inc = ->(x) { x + 1 }
dbl = ->(x) { x * 2 }
puts compose.(inc, dbl).(5)
puts (inc >> dbl).call(5), (inc << dbl).call(5)
puts %w[a b].each_with_index.map { |s, i| "#{i}#{s}" }.inspect
```

What does this print?
```ruby
def f
  yield 1, 2
end
f { |a| puts a.inspect }
f { |a, b| puts [a, b].inspect }
f { |*all| puts all.inspect }
pr = proc { |a, b| [a, b] }
puts pr.call([5, 6]).inspect
```
